 I  hope that they'll find the time to do  that either by giving her a little bit  of her own arc because in series 11 you  know Graham and Ryan had an arc yes  didn't really so maybe they'll do that  or maybe they'll just find a function  she serves within the group that none of  the others fulfill  I would hope her background as a police  officer would in some way factor into  that and certainly give some groundwork  to do it but they haven't yet and I  really hope they do especially since  they're keeping a rabid crowd and TARDIS  if we kind of keep this many around have  a reason for them to be there so that's  the first one next up I really want them  to make the TARDIS feel like a home  again there's a couple of things that  contribute to this in series 11 the  TARDIS first of all we spent very little  time in there it was just it just got us  from place to place it never felt like  the home base that they returned to it  was just the vehicle and it didn't help  how darkly lit it was it didn't feel  like a place you would want to be a  place where you would want to just dwell  because the preet the other iterations  of the TARDIS that we've had in modern  era Doctor Who not all of them felt  super homey I would argue Matt Smith's  first TARDIS was the most felt like a  home especially with you know when he  had Amy and Rory and they kept coming  back there and spent a lot of time in  there but even going back to classic era  Doctor Who they would spend more time in  the console room that's where they would  come back to meet the doctor and the  companions and it never felt like  anybody wanted to get back inside the  TARDIS during series 11 other than like  that very first moment of them finding  it in the ghost Wineman that was a great  moment but after that it was basically  just their ride and nothing else and the  TARDIS should be more than that  and I kind of hope they'll they'll build  that up a little bit better next up okay  I need more focus on the doctor this is  another upshot of the fact that I don't  think it was a good idea to introduce a  four person TARDIS crew in a series  where we didn't know any of these  characters already especially a series  with fewer episodes I didn't feel like I  got this doctor I didn't feel like I  understood what Jodi Whitaker's approach  really was until the very end of series  11 and that frustrated me and I think  part of the reason that I felt that was  because she was sharing basically equal  time with the companions now that's not  inherently a bad thing but it did mean I  felt like out of those four the  characters who I understood best were  Ryan and Graham and while they're good  characters and I'm happy to know them  I'm here for the doctor I want to know  what this doctor so I want to get a  better sense of her I want her to be  more focused more front-and-center  deal more with how things affect her  directly because it felt like almost  everything got filtered through the  companions in some way in the previous  series and I'm not gonna say that didn't  work for some stories that worked very  well but I want more of the doctor  herself please give it to me all right  what else have I got  oh all right this is a minor nitpick you  want I really hope Jody but it could  change the way she's wielding the sonic  screwdriver because look plenty of  people made fun of Matt Smith treating  it like a magic wand cuz he was like  whoa honestly that didn't bother me all  that much and that never felt nearly as  much like a magic wand as does I hate  this big arm arch I hate this big  exaggerated motion it's a tool bring it  up and use it generally if you use it  it's cuz you need it don't do this  stop just don't that's a minor one but  it bugged me all right what else have I  got okay the last two are basically  interconnected so I'll lump them  together don't throw out everything  different you did in series 11 and don't  immediately bring back everything you  didn't use in